From 72fa57718a1b947bcbf75dd552034a120c10464e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSwetz <Johnswetz1982@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:40:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(motion): give collapsed open chamfer run its own
 refusal message

In 2D open chamfer, an open run that collapses to fewer than two distinct points now returns an explicit chamfer refusal. It does not return the generic centerline refusal message.

The defensive guard in chamfer_open_runs is documented. Tests for open chamfer refusals are moved to their own test binary, keeping chamfer_circular within the line limit.

Pinned by an_open_chamfer_collapsing_to_one_point_refuses_by_name, an_open_chamfer_with_a_collapsed_segment_refuses_by_name, and an_open_chamfer_without_a_model_wall_refuses_by_name.

